<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Akassa raid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1895">1895</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Akassa raid was an attack on 29 January 1895 by warriors of the Nembe kingdom of Brass, led by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-william-koko">Frederick William Koko</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-niger-company">Royal Niger Company</a>'s depot at Akassa in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> delta. Protesting the company's exclusion of Nembe traders from the Niger markets, they killed and captured dozens of company employees. British forces retaliated by burning Nembe, and the affair contributed to the end of the company's charter in 1900.</p></div>
